{
  "_notes": [
    "Back to the Future [Data East, 1990]",
    "2026-02-14 added by Tom Collins <tom@scorbit.io>",
    "Adjustments 0x1E00-0x1E42 are protected by a plain 8-bit sum (checksum8_sum, not complemented) at 0x1EDE,",
    "the byte right after the custom-message text, followed by a change counter and the 0xFF fill. This",
    "block runs from 0x1E00 to the byte before the 0xFF fill. Verified against saved bttf_a27 images (both cabinets), one",
    "writer must drop the write rather than repair it.",
    "Adjustments 0x1E00-0x1E42 are protected by a plain 8-bit sum (complement false) at 0x1EDE; see README.md in maps/dataeast.",
    "The declaration follows bttf_a27 and bttf_g27, whose ROMs sum 0x1E00-0x1E42 and which is the revision confirmed against saved NVRAM. bttf_a28 itself sums one byte more, 0x1E00-0x1E43."
  ],
